Z||000000||AusFiero||09-14-2001||08:01 PM||||Well the owner of the t-topped SE just wont return phone calls so I went looking for another Fiero and found this. <BR>$11,000 or about US$5600<BR>86 SE<BR>15" GT Rims<BR>4 Speed V6<BR>36,000 Miles on the clock<BR>Moon Roof. <BR>Competition Suspension (sway bars and aftermarket shocks etc)<BR>Improved Brakes (crossdrilled rotors etc)<BR>1 owner, as new condition.<P>Now the dilema. I wanted a custom Fiero. 3.8 litr SC Buick, my fasback panels, my 5 speed box, custom interior etc. Would you guys butcher a car with this many miles on the clock. Or should I just buy it and leave it original? Well then again it isn't really original to start with is it. Hmmmmmmm decisions are hard.<BR><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||09-14-2001||08:26 PM||||G'day, Jim!!  I'd buy the car (assuming it's worth it) and modify it to your tastes.  36k miles isn't <I>that</I> low.  Now, if you had a car like mrfiero just sold (271 mile Formula?), I'd leave it alone.  Do your best work on it and use it as a sales tool for your interior stuff and Stage 2 kit.||||reg||1
Z||000002||California Kid||09-14-2001||08:46 PM||||Hey Jim....Hard to say, don't know how good the pickins' are done there. Sounds like an excellent base car though.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rick 88||09-15-2001||12:43 AM||||Aus,<P>You can only make it better!<P>Rick<BR>yellow 88 GT 5-speed||||reg||10
Z||000004||Cheever3000||09-15-2001||01:08 AM||||Jim, to anyone else I would say don't touch it.  But like Rick88 says, <I>you</I> would only make it better!  In your hands, well, it's no worries, as far as I'm concerned.  <P>(And just where <I>is</I> Snowy River, anyway?)<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Leper||09-15-2001||02:10 AM||||Yeah, completely deck it out with your wares, then use it as a billboard for your company. Sell the parts that you don't need and maybe try and make it a t-top car.<P>As long as it doesn't end up looking like that hooptie lowrider Fiero on Ebay. It should be great.||||reg||1
Z||000006||AusFiero||09-15-2001||03:06 AM||||Yes I seen that horrible looking lowrider one. Isn't it disgusting. <BR>Now I am even more confused. Have rang about 2 other options I can get. 1 is an 88 Formula with t-tops, but he will fit it with a GT nose for me and overhaul it mechanically including fitting a 3.8 litre Holden V6 and give the car a mechanical warranty. That car is an auto which I find appealing due to the pedal locations in converted cars. The other is also really apealling because it is an 86 that requires a new engine and gearbox but comes with a Ferrari 308 GTS rebody with new paint getting done this week and new mags and tyres fitted. That one I could fit my engine and gearbox too and stay in budget. <P>Help me guys/gals. It is getting confusing which is the best option now. Either way I have my t-tops to fit to whichever car and my seats and doortrims are salvageable (with a good clean). I thought they was dead but they can be cleaned it seems. <P>Oh god it is hard. <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||09-15-2001||05:06 AM||||I'd go for the Formula.  With an aero front fascia and your fastback clip/rear fascia, you'll basically have what you have now, but with the drivetrain you really want.  Add your Stage 2 kit when it's ready and truely have a unique car.  I don't know how you are with mechanical things, but we all know how you do with body work.  If you really want a 308, you could always make one yourself in the future for a lot less (just a guess) than you could find/rebuild/install a V6 Holden/auto tranny.  You could sell your current powertrain to recoup some of the loss.  (I'd be happy to take that Getrag off your hands!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )  Any way you go, please keep us informed.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Indiana_resto_guy||09-15-2001||08:11 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AusFiero:<BR><B><BR>Now I am even more confused. Have rang about 2 other options I can get. 1 is an 88 Formula with t-tops, but he will fit it with a GT nose for me and overhaul it mechanically including fitting a 3.8 litre Holden V6 and give the car a mechanical warranty. That car is an auto which I find appealing due to the pedal locations in converted cars. The other is also really apealling because it is an 86 that requires a new engine and gearbox but comes with a Ferrari 308 GTS rebody with new paint getting done this week and new mags and tyres fitted. That one I could fit my engine and gearbox too and stay in budget. <P>Help me guys/gals. It is getting confusing which is the best option now. Either way I have my t-tops to fit to whichever car and my seats and doortrims are salvageable (with a good clean). I thought they was dead but they can be cleaned it seems. <P>Oh god it is hard. <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, since your 88 isn't as wasted as you first thought why not rebuild it and get the 308 GTS rebody?<P>If you don't go that way and buy the GTS rebody and not a stock appearing Fiero be sort of tough fitting the Stage II kit to it, right? <BR>Does the GTS retain the Fieros roof line for T-Tops?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Rick 88||09-15-2001||09:20 AM||||Jim,<P>After taking another look at the pics of your car I wonder how much it would need. I would love to see your nose redesign on this car. There are a number of vented hood designs you could whip up. Body panels are readily available. You could get wiring harnessess from Ed Parks or Kick Hill Farms. I think FieroDave was even selling a complete low mileage 88 front suspension drop out for $450.00 if yours can't be rebuilt. <P>Just a thought. Why don't you compile a list of parts you need and post it to the forum.<P>Just my .02 cents,<P>Rick 88||||reg||3
Z||000010||AusFiero||09-15-2001||09:26 AM||||See the mall rick... I have  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Well I ahve decided I am buying the other 86 regardless...the guy who owns it is a rich car enthusiast who has spent mega bucks on it. Found out tonight it is also lowered and has lots of little extras he didn't mention the first chat. All this stuff costs big bucks here. The other I may still fix also.||||reg||1
